WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.269
-My first guest tonight
is on Oscar-nominated actor

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:06.739
who stars in the new movie
"Hitman's Wife's Bodyguard,"

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:08.040
which is in theaters tomorrow.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.510
Here is Salma Hayek!

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.811
Yeah!

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:13.012
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:15.447
Come on.
Oh, so happy to see you.

00:00:15.447 --> 00:00:19.185
Salma!
-Jimmy!

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:21.521
-Ah. Thank you so much
for coming on the show.

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:25.224
I appreciate it.
I follow you on Instagram.

00:00:25.224 --> 00:00:26.392
And it's --
You're a good follow.

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:27.660
And you're really fun.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.862
I just thought this was
very interesting here

00:00:29.862 --> 00:00:31.364
on your bio here.

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:33.500
If you see -- It's all emojis.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.367
-[ Laughter ]
-Yes.

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:38.237
'Cause you're supposed to
describe yourself.

00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:42.942
And I'm lazy trying to,
you know, philosophize

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:45.912
and come up with a couple
of sentences about who I am,

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:48.448
so instead
I just picked all the emojis

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:50.583
that have anything
to do with my life.

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:52.952
And that represents who I am.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.987
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.987 --> 00:00:57.023
-Wow. A lot of things.

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:59.425
There's an octopus on here.

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:01.728
Can you explain the octopus?

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:03.696
-Yes. I'm a diver.

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:07.967
And so I have most
of the aquatic animals.

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:12.505
And I remember -- I've had
some encounters with octopus.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:16.942
One that I really remember,
very clearly, is an octopus

00:01:16.942 --> 00:01:22.415
that came and went on my mask
and started exploring me.

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:24.516
And you cannot panic.
-Wait.

00:01:24.516 --> 00:01:27.720
-And you have to, like,
bite down on your bite

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.890
because they can pull it out,
or the mask.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.492
And it was so weird what I was
seeing at the beginning.

00:01:33.492 --> 00:01:35.662
Then it goes black.

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:39.032
But it was kind of magical
seeing it.

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:41.567
-Oh, my God.
-And then he went away.

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:44.404
I remember dating guys like that
when I was younger.

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:46.038
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.038 --> 00:01:48.774
-Oh, my God. Oh, my --

00:01:48.774 --> 00:01:50.810
Thank goodness
those days are over.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.579
-...lot of memories...
-Yeah.

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:55.981
-You know, can I tell you
something really random

00:01:55.981 --> 00:01:57.450
that I just remember?

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:01.387
My brother -- I don't know.
He used to call them Octopussy.

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:03.323
And I'm like,
"That's not a word."

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:05.892
But he kept
calling them Octopussy,

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:07.493
which is very inappropriate.

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:10.263
Never mind.
We're done with the Octopussies.

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.031
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:15.735
-No, that's a James Bond film.
Sure, it's a word. Sure.

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:18.137
If we were playing Scrabble,
I'll give him the points.

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:21.006
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.006 --> 00:02:24.410
Also, you're in this
giant Marvel movie, "Eternals,"

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.446
and it just got announced,
and the trailer came out.

00:02:27.446 --> 00:02:30.650
It broke the Internet in half.
Were you psyched?

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:33.419
I mean, did you go, "Oh, yeah.
I know how to do this."

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:36.122
Is it like another action --
I know you've done action films.

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:39.492
-No. I was shocked.
Can you imagine?

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:43.963
You get a superhero character
in your fifties?!

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:47.266
Mexican. Woman. In your fifties?

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:49.902
-Yeah. For you.
I would see you do anything.

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:53.039
You can do anything!
-I couldn't believe it.

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:55.174
-But did you have
any superhero moments?

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:57.276
You're in the movie,
and you got a -- whew! --

00:02:57.276 --> 00:02:59.044
or a green-screen thing
or something?

00:02:59.044 --> 00:03:02.382
Are you on wires?
What are you doing?

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:05.451
-My most exciting moment --

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:08.020
It was very unexpected.

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:12.492
Because there are superhero
moments, but the coolest one

00:03:12.492 --> 00:03:16.663
was galloping in a meadow
with a horse.

00:03:16.663 --> 00:03:18.865
And that's when
I thought to myself,

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:22.201
"Not only I'm doing
a Marvel superhero movie,

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:26.338
but I'm doing, like,
a really different, cool one."

00:03:26.338 --> 00:03:28.474
-See? When we see that scene...

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:31.276
When we see that scene,
I'm gonna be clapping for you.

00:03:31.276 --> 00:03:33.179
I love it.

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:36.482
This week, you star in
"Hitman's Wife's Bodyguard."

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:40.453
This is two of our favorites.
Ryan Reynolds and Sam Jackson.

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:44.657
Congrats. This is the second
one. They wanted more of you.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:46.993
They wanted more of you.

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:50.029
So, yeah -- So you got
your own spin-off kind of.

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:52.431
-Kind of --
Well, it wouldn't have been

00:03:52.431 --> 00:03:54.166
so hard to get more of me

00:03:54.166 --> 00:03:56.402
because I only worked two days
on the first one.

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:58.171
-Yeah.
-But I was very lucky 'cause

00:03:58.171 --> 00:04:01.808
now I worked the entire movie
on this one.

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:04.977
And I have to say
that I started practicing

00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:07.279
saying the name of the movie
since we were shooting it.

00:04:07.279 --> 00:04:10.049
Because I am dyslexic.

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:12.985
And "Hitman's Bodyguard Wife,"

00:04:12.985 --> 00:04:15.221
"Hitman's Wife Bodyguard,"
"Bodyguard's Wife's Hitman."

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:18.591
I mean, I get really confused.
-"Hitman's Wife's Bodyguard."

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:20.727
"Hitman's Wife's Bodyguard."

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:22.928
-Bodyguard, yeah.
-Yeah, exactly right. Yeah.

00:04:22.928 --> 00:04:25.898
And you play the hitman's wife.

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.600
-Exactly.
-That's right. Exactly.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.068
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:32.037
And Sam plays --
Sam Jackson plays the hitman.

00:04:32.037 --> 00:04:34.706
And Ryan Reynolds
is our bodyguard.

00:04:34.706 --> 00:04:36.709
-God, he is so funny.

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:41.347
There's a lot of swearing
in this film.

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:43.149
I'm surprised.
Samuel L. Jackson.

00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:44.717
I know the --

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:47.586
But I was going to ask you --
'Cause I rarely hear you swear.

00:04:47.586 --> 00:04:50.590
Did it rub off
on the real Salma Hayek?

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.892
-Oh, completely. Completely.

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:56.595
I have to be very careful
because I still have

00:04:56.595 --> 00:04:59.732
a little bit of Sonia
that comes out here and there.

00:04:59.732 --> 00:05:01.500
And I have my daughter.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:05.671
And one time, I was just --
She just went, "Mom!"

00:05:05.671 --> 00:05:08.774
And I said, "Oh, it was not me.
It was Sonia."

00:05:08.774 --> 00:05:11.077
-Yeah. That's good, yeah.
-So now I use it every time

00:05:11.077 --> 00:05:13.079
that I say something
that I shouldn't say.

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:15.014
I just say, "It was not me.
It was Sonia."

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:17.283
-Yeah, and it's kind of fun

00:05:17.283 --> 00:05:20.919
to have a curse conversation

00:05:20.919 --> 00:05:23.089
with Samuel L. Jackson,
isn't it?

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:24.557
-Well, it's fun,

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:26.191
but it was very intimidating
at the beginning.

00:05:26.191 --> 00:05:28.327
-The best.

00:05:28.327 --> 00:05:30.529
-I was like Robert De Niro
in "Taxi Driver"

00:05:30.529 --> 00:05:35.701
in front of the mirror
practicing my "mother..."

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:38.437
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Yeah, yeah, uh-huh.

00:05:38.437 --> 00:05:40.840
-You know, because I have to
say it in front of him

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:43.209
a lot of times,
and it's quite intimidating.

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:44.843
-Yeah, yeah. It's good.

00:05:44.843 --> 00:05:46.679
Well, we had a hard time
finding a clip

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:48.414
because there's so much cursing.

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:51.284
No, no. I'm joking.
I'm joking. It's very funny.

00:05:51.284 --> 00:05:53.819
It's action-packed.
We have a clip.

00:05:53.819 --> 00:05:56.755
Here's Salma Hayek in
"Hitman's Wife's Bodyguard."

00:05:56.755 --> 00:05:58.023
Take a look at this.

00:05:58.023 --> 00:05:59.625
-Come on! Let's go!

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.193
[ Engine revs ]

00:06:01.193 --> 00:06:03.162
♪♪

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:04.763
[ Indistinct shouting ]

00:06:04.763 --> 00:06:06.165
-Take the gun.

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:07.967
-No, I'm not doing guns
right now.

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:09.434
[ Tires screech ]

00:06:09.434 --> 00:06:11.070
-I got it.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.872
♪♪

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:14.673
[ Gunfire ]

00:06:14.673 --> 00:06:21.914
♪♪

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:29.121
♪♪

00:06:29.121 --> 00:06:31.090
Wait, wait, wait!
No, no, no, no, no!

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:32.591
There's got to be
a safer way down.

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:34.127
There's got to be
a safer way down.

00:06:34.127 --> 00:06:35.528
There's maybe like a switch --
Okay.

00:06:35.528 --> 00:06:37.730
[ Laughter ]

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.732
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-See?

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:42.969
-That's right! Come on!
Always bringing it.

00:06:42.969 --> 00:06:45.571
We love you.
Salma Hayek, everybody.

